Subject: [PATCH 08614/11362] Phase 4b: internal held-out check does not fix
 nav gate's cd82 gap (negative)

Follow-up to REQ-ARC-WMTE-6244's cd82 false positive: tried hardening
is_confident_nav with a train/held-out generalization check. Built it,
tested against the known true positive (tu93) BEFORE committing, and found
it also scores 0.0 -- not a fitting bug (train-only refit's structural
params for tu93 are fully correct) but the same HUD/step-counter
contamination this project's own structured_nav_heldout comment already
names. Switched to changed-cell recall (the metric already preferred for
that reason): does not rescue it either -- cd82 (0.507) and wa30 (0.823,
a known false positive) both score at or above tu93 (0.417).

Reverted the code change before committing anything. Recorded as a negative
result (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6245) per the Failed-Experiment Rerun Discipline, so a
future retry does not re-walk the same two metrics at the same sample size.
is_confident_nav's three existing structural checks are unchanged.

determination_preservation_lint, adversarial_verify, artifact_freshness_lint
all clean.
